e used for documentation. local comment should use //"]],0,428],[7198366,20417,21,0.634,0.471,[[0,0.52,379,10],[1,0.48,7,11]],[["ecc12cd5_e1653dc4",49,-1,1,"this is fusebox-specific, not tab picker-specific, correct? seems to be recorded _after_ user completes selection with the tab picker? what if the user dismisses the tab picker? please document this…"]],0,429],[7209213,20420,20,0.634,0.471,[[0,380]],[],0,430],[7209207,20423,225,4.044,3.245,[[0,0.894,381,202],[9,0.106,0,23]],[["6f7bee40_63cdcf75",46,-3,0,"Do we notify session abandoned on successful queries ?"],["166bac0e_9c930134",46,0,1,"You can use `kAdobePortableDocumentFormatMimeType` from `ios/chrome/browser/shared/model/utils/mime_type_util.h` here."],["630a668b_e586927d",46,0,1,"nit: remove this `const` (or change the type to `const base::UnguessableToken&`)."],["67b9d26c_bbfd993c",50,0,1,"Since `ContextualSearchService` is a `KeyedService` which has a different factory in `//chrome/browser` and `//ios/chrome/browser`, it is possible to avoid this `#if BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS)` check here.…"],["6df00534_e6e7e8fe",17,0,1,"It is possible to avoid this warning by splitting the CL in multiple parts. At least one part adding the `KeyedService` factory in ios/chrome/browser, one part doing the renaming `token` ->…"],["7757e1fc_d57ea85d",46,0,1,"ditto, remove `const`"],["a9209d1d_edff5fe6",51,0,1,"This is here that you would control how `ContextualSearchService` creates the `ComposeboxQueryController`. Either yoy have and `IOSContextualSearchService` that sub-classes `ContextualSearchSearvice`…"],["ae1bcb5a_585890a7",46,0,1,"ditto"],["b8e5ae73_16ba656b",52,0,1,"`//components/omnibox/composebox` depends on `//components/contextual_search`: ``` $ $ git grep components/contextual_search -- components/omnibox/composebox…"],["f06c83fb_6b7fc2a2",46,0,1,"You mix `base::UnguessableToken`, `const base::UnguessableToken` and `const base::UnguessableToken&` in this file. Please fix and use `const base::UnguessableToken&` consistently (or optionally…"],["f7d88d5b_0d249155",46,0,0,"Move this into the `if (_contextualSearchSession)` block since this is only used there. Additionally, `mojo_base::BigBuffer` constructor accepts a `base::span<const uint8_t>` as input and always copy…"],["fee84294_b73978e6",46,0,1,"ditto, here and everywhere else in this file (I will stop pointing at individual occurrences)"]],0,431],[7213678,20423,442,6.365,5.105,[[0,0.949,382,423],[10,0.051,0,19]],[],0,432],[7216128,20424,39,1.122,0.86,[[0,0.795,383,32],[4,0.205,18,7]],[],0,433],[7213565,20424,15,0.494,0.286,[[4,0.556,19,9],[11,0.444,4,6]],[["35ed33aa_9e264edb",53,-1,1,"should iOS eventually have its own page classifications? Also why do we need to return the contextual searchbox page classification if there are attachments? This gets handled later on for…"],["64faf755_0e311f14",15,-1,1,"Why not keep this NTP_COMPOSEBOX, comments in `composebox_omnibox_client.mm` still apply, regarding creating a new page classification for iOS"],["ebfbe4ee_da3f905a",54,-1,0,"Why is this needed? Won't other results not show already if we're going to be returning the verbatim match only?"],["df7f69a8_2394e086",54,0,0,"qq: This won't affect the desktop implementation since we hide the dropdown in this case for now right? But desktop will need to enable this flag if we ever want context typed suggestions?"],["ecc4e502_37d26d19",54,3,0,"This broke the Lens side panel suggestions on Chrome desktop. Why are we adding a universal flag instead of letting each feature control this behavior?"]],0,434],[7222430,20425,86,2.087,1.667,[[0,384]],[],0,435],[7222930,20425,62,1.122,0.86,[[0,0.758,385,47],[2,0.242,12,15]],[],0,436],[7224050,20426,14,0.451,0.316,[[0,386]],[["f00e6ff3_09064a10",46,0,0,"Why removing this?"]],0,437],[7232071,20427,2,0.147,0.096,[[0,387]],[],0,438],[7233230,20427,10,0.451,0.316,[[0,388]],[["75daa6b2_3345e99d",46,0,1,"navigation can also happen here"],["ee0c474a_e56d011b",46,0,1,"reset innavigation here"]],0,439],[723449